/* Main computational kernel. The whole function will be timed,
   including the call and return.
 *
 * Optimizations:
 *  - Use a single OpenMP parallel region around all four loops to
 *    amortize threading overhead and exploit 32 cores.
 *  - Parallelize all outer i-loops; each iteration updates a distinct
 *    row (or vector element), so there are no data races.
 *  - Improve data locality by keeping inner loops over the contiguous
 *    dimension of A (the column index j when using A[i][j]).
 *  - Introduce row-local pointers (Ai) and scalar accumulators (xi, wi)
 *    to reduce repeated address calculations and memory traffic.
 *  - Hoist per-row invariants (u1[i], u2[i]) outside the inner loop.
 *  - Keep the algebraic form and loop traversal order per element
 *    identical, so the sequence of operations for each scalar variable
 *    is preserved.
